        <p class="profile-detail-region">Life · Central &amp; East Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Genghis Khan</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1162 CE – 1227 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1162 (historians also favour 1155 or 1167), at Delüün Boldog on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onon-river">Onon River</a> according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/secret-history-of-the-mongols">Secret History of the Mongols</a>; eldest child of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yesugei">Yesügei</a>, a chieftain of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borjigin">Borjigin</a> clan, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoelun">Hö'elün</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">18 or 25 August 1227, during the siege of the Western Xia capital Zhongxing, after months of illness following a fall from his horse; the exact cause is disputed</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Khan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> (acclaimed by his followers before c. 1187); Genghis Khan, first khan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>, 1206–1227</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Uniting the tribes of the Mongolian steppe; founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>; reorganising Mongol society into a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/decimal-military-organisation">decimal military system</a>; the conquest of the Jin capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhongdu">Zhongdu</a>; the destruction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmian-empire">Khwarazmian Empire</a>; campaigns that killed millions; a trading system spanning <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eurasia">Eurasia</a></span></div>
